    "updated_at": "2020-09-21T06:49:46Z",
    "body": "I second this proposal. It doesn't look good if you have any custom module. As you can see that I have a custom docker icon module.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24727447/93738374-3efb9d00-fc03-11ea-9d6a-f0b7a81e67c0.png)\r\n\r\nOne way to fix this using `prompt_order` but as @badnetmask @matchai said It is not perfect. And the other is disable `cmd_duration` which is I am doing currently.\r\n\r\nIMO `cmd_duration` should come after `custom` as `cmd_duration` is shown temporarily. And It will look good if something is removed from last rather than something in between.\r\n\r\n- With `custom` before `cmd_duration`\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24727447/93738863-79196e80-fc04-11ea-8d73-f2fdae89c94d.png)\r\n\r\n- After `cmd_duration` is gone\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24727447/93738896-8f272f00-fc04-11ea-99bf-ee80bfee18c7.png)\r\n",
