    "updated_at": "2021-03-21T18:13:33Z",
    "body": "I was looking for a way to move the Time module to the first line of my prompt, and I think it'd be good to have an easier way to move individual modules around in general.\r\n\r\nIf I'm understanding the comments here and the documentation, this is the default `format` (found here: https://starship.rs/config/#prompt):\r\n\r\n```\r\nformat = \"\"\"\r\n$username\\\r\n$hostname\\\r\n$shlvl\\\r\n$kubernetes\\\r\n$directory\\\r\n$git_branch\\\r\n$git_commit\\\r\n$git_state\\\r\n$git_status\\\r\n$hg_branch\\\r\n$docker_context\\\r\n$package\\\r\n$cmake\\\r\n$dart\\\r\n$dotnet\\\r\n$elixir\\\r\n$elm\\\r\n$erlang\\\r\n$golang\\\r\n$helm\\\r\n$java\\\r\n$julia\\\r\n$kotlin\\\r\n$nim\\\r\n$nodejs\\\r\n$ocaml\\\r\n$perl\\\r\n$php\\\r\n$purescript\\\r\n$python\\\r\n$ruby\\\r\n$rust\\\r\n$swift\\\r\n$terraform\\\r\n$vagrant\\\r\n$zig\\\r\n$nix_shell\\\r\n$conda\\\r\n$memory_usage\\\r\n$aws\\\r\n$gcloud\\\r\n$openstack\\\r\n$env_var\\\r\n$crystal\\\r\n$custom\\\r\n$cmd_duration\\\r\n$line_break\\\r\n$lua\\\r\n$jobs\\\r\n$battery\\\r\n$time\\\r\n$status\\\r\n$character\"\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd currently, to move the Time module to the first line, that must be changed to:\r\n\r\n```\r\nformat = \"\"\"\r\n$username\\\r\n$hostname\\\r\n$shlvl\\\r\n$kubernetes\\\r\n$directory\\\r\n$git_branch\\\r\n$git_commit\\\r\n$git_state\\\r\n$git_status\\\r\n$hg_branch\\\r\n$docker_context\\\r\n$package\\\r\n$cmake\\\r\n$dart\\\r\n$dotnet\\\r\n$elixir\\\r\n$elm\\\r\n$erlang\\\r\n$golang\\\r\n$helm\\\r\n$java\\\r\n$julia\\\r\n$kotlin\\\r\n$nim\\\r\n$nodejs\\\r\n$ocaml\\\r\n$perl\\\r\n$php\\\r\n$purescript\\\r\n$python\\\r\n$ruby\\\r\n$rust\\\r\n$swift\\\r\n$terraform\\\r\n$vagrant\\\r\n$zig\\\r\n$nix_shell\\\r\n$conda\\\r\n$memory_usage\\\r\n$aws\\\r\n$gcloud\\\r\n$openstack\\\r\n$env_var\\\r\n$crystal\\\r\n$custom\\\r\n$cmd_duration\\\r\n$time\\\r\n$line_break\\\r\n$lua\\\r\n$jobs\\\r\n$battery\\\r\n$status\\\r\n$character\"\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n(or similar)\r\n\r\n> I basically need to copy the entire default value into my config, and make the one single change that I care about\r\n\r\n> my local config will be fixed in time, and will never take into consideration additions/removals of modules, or changes in the default order, unless I keep tracking the changes in GitHub\r\n\r\nI totally agree with these points!\r\n\r\nSorry, I don't have an idea (yet?) for how to solve this problem. But I wanted to refresh the issue cause the previously mentioned `prompt_order` option appears to have been removed.",
