    "created_at": "2021-03-23T17:42:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-23T17:42:38Z",
    "body": "Agreed, I have a custom time module that I needed to add after the existing time module so I could format it differently after work hours.\r\n\r\nI just updated and grabbed the latest format config to re-insert my custom.time, and found several new modules had been added. I can continue doing so, as I'm tracking my config as part of my dotfiles repo, but the issue is real!\r\n\r\nHaving a `before`/`after` config value for each item would have been great with `prompt_order` to insert relative to other modules, but that won't work with the current `format` option, as that's just an interpolated string now, [prompt_order was removed with 0.45.0](https://starship.rs/migrating-to-0.45.0/#prompt-order-has-been-replaced-by-a-root-level-format).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
